{
  "page_id": "SR-26",
  "section_header": "STEERING — Power Steering",
  "title": "INSTALLATION OF POWER STEERING PUMP",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(See page SR-18)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "1. INSTALL POWER STEERING PUMP"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "(a) Place the PS pump in position and torque the front mount bolt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "torque_spec",
      "component": "Front mount bolt",
      "value": "375 kg-cm (27 ft-lb, 37 N·m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "(b) Install the drive belt adjust bolt by hand."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 1,
      "description": "Power steering pump assembly showing pump unit with mounting bracket and drive belt",
      "labels": [
        "Power steering pump",
        "Drive belt"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 5,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 37,
        "height": 18
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "2. INSTALL PULLEY AND DRIVE BELT"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "(a) Install the woodruff key and pulley.",
        "(b) Install the pulley set nut.",
        "(c) Install the drive belt.",
        "(d) Insert a bar under the PS pump and ply it upward until the belt tension is at specified value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Belt tension gauge:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "caption": "Belt tension gauge specifications",
      "headers": [
        "Manufacturer",
        "Part Number"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Nippondenso",
          "BTG-20 (95606-00020) or"
        ],
        [
          "Borroughs",
          "No. BT-33-73F"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Drive belt tension:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "caption": "Drive belt tension specifications",
      "headers": [
        "Belt Condition",
        "Tension"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "New belt",
          "125 ÷ 25 lb"
        ],
        [
          "Used belt",
          "80 ÷ 20 lb"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "notice",
      "text": "NOTE:\n• \"New belt\" refers to a brand new belt which has never before been used.\n• \"Used belt\" refers to a belt which has been used on a running engine for 5 minutes or more."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "(e) Torque the adjust bolt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "torque_spec",
      "component": "Adjust bolt",
      "value": "375 kg-cm (27 ft-lb, 37 N·m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "(f) Push down on the drive belt to hold the pulley in place and torque the pulley set nut."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "torque_spec",
      "component": "Pulley set nut",
      "value": "445 kg-cm (32 ft-lb, 44 N·m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "(g) Install and torque the PS pump rear mount bolt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "torque_spec",
      "component": "PS pump rear mount bolt",
      "value": "375 kg-cm (27 ft-lb, 37 N·m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 2,
      "description": "Power steering pump with pulley and drive belt installed, showing woodruff key and pulley assembly",
      "labels": [
        "Pulley",
        "Drive belt",
        "Woodruff key"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 24,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 37,
        "height": 18
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 3,
      "description": "Belt tension measurement setup showing Nippondenso and Borroughs tension gauges positioned on drive belt between pulleys",
      "labels": [
        "Nippondenso",
        "Borroughs"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 43,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 37,
        "height": 18
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "3. CONNECT PRESSURE TUBE TO POWER STEERING PUMP"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Using SST, connect and torque the pressure tube."
    },
    {
      "type": "part_number",
      "label": "SST",
      "number": "09631-22020",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "torque_spec",
      "component": "Pressure tube",
      "value": "450 kg-cm (33 ft-lb, 44 N·m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 4,
      "description": "Connection of pressure tube to power steering pump using SST tool",
      "labels": [
        "SST",
        "Pressure tube"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 62,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 37,
        "height": 18
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "4. CONNECT RETURN HOSE TO RESERVOIR TANK"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "5. CONNECT AIR HOSES TO AIR CONTROL VALVE"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "6. FILL RESERVOIR WITH FLUID"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Fluid: ATF DEXRON® or DEXRON® II"
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 5,
      "description": "Filling power steering reservoir with fluid using funnel",
      "labels": [
        "Reservoir",
        "Fluid"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 81,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 37,
        "height": 18
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "7. BLEED POWER STEERING"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "8. CHECK FOR FLUID LEAKS"
    }
  ]
}
